# Summoner — one of the Henchmen of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 10/12 The Henchmen — up to 27 life, can't be bribed
# enemy: Summoner (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0030.dck "Summoner (G/W, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 13 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 14 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/summoner.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 10)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/summoner.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Henchmen) — "Summoner" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Summoner
20 Forest
4 Plains
2 Colossus of Sardia
4 Birds of Paradise
4 Lifelace
1 Channel
3 Circle of Protection: Green
4 Hurricane
4 War Mammoth
3 Force of Nature
2 Disenchant
2 Healing Salve
4 Radjan Spirit
3 Giant Growth
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Giant Growth
#   .vBlack  2 Giant Growth, 1 Lifeforce
#   .vBlue   2 Giant Growth, 1 Tsunami
#   .vGreen  3 Giant Growth
#   .vRed    3 Giant Growth
#   .vWhite  2 Giant Growth, 1 Disenchant
SB: 1 Lifeforce
SB: 1 Tsunami
SB: 1 Disenchant
